# CI-002 — Hivemind functionality isn't yet refined and interoperable

**Aspiration:** [Share without surrendering control](../pillars/compounding-intelligence.md#share-without-surrendering-control) (primary) · [Built to be found and reused](../principles/open-by-design.md#built-to-be-found-and-reused) (supporting) · [Explicit permissions and privacy](../principles/in-the-creators-control.md#explicit-permissions-and-privacy) (supporting) · **Assessment:** Open, proposal compared with source (2026-11-06).

## Desired state

Independent personal, team and community knowledge datasets can preserve attribution, conditions, evidence and owner-controlled access while exchanging permitted references and learnings without merging into one central authority.

## Current state

[Banodoco Hivemind](../../plans/22-hivemind-protocol/inputs.md) documents source-custodied messages, revisioned resources, an accepted search head and editorial contribution operations. The [uploaded October 29 protocol proposal](../../plans/22-hivemind-protocol/protocol-proposal.md) proposes dataset-scoped entries, typed links and `find`/`inspect`/`contribute`. **These are not yet identical proven contracts.**

## Gap

Hivemind's existing functionality and proposed protocol still need refinement and real proof: stable versioned identities, useful references, access decisions and scoped exchange between independently owned datasets. Public-source ingestion belongs to [CI-003](CI-003-public-source-ingestion.md), rather than being rolled into this gap.

## Closure evidence

Two separately owned datasets can exchange a scoped, independently attributed reference or approved sanitized result, preserving revision identity, provenance and access decisions; denied, stale and revoked cases do not leak source content. Banodoco behavior is preserved or safely, explicitly migrated with evidence.

## Sources and reassessment

[Current Hivemind source map](../../plans/22-hivemind-protocol/inputs.md) · [Dated protocol proposal](../../plans/22-hivemind-protocol/protocol-proposal.md). Source claims in the proposal, including migration and privacy assertions, require verification; a draft spec is not implementation proof.
